WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:02.110
INTRO:
Remember Mythbusters?

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:07.240
Throughout the 2000s and early 2010s, Mythbusters
was one of the most popular science based

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.590
shows in the entire world.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:14.070
Every week, we got to see the cast put popular
myths and urban legends to the test.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.920
Is it likely that the Alcatraz prison escape
was successful?

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:22.449
If you drink diet coke and instantly eat mentos
right after, would your stomach explode?

00:00:22.449 --> 00:00:27.269
And most importantly, could Jack and Rose
have shared the door in Titanic?

00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:30.539
Myths like these kept many of addicted to
the show for several years.

00:00:30.539 --> 00:00:36.000
But, out of nowhere, in late 2015, the Mythbusters
announced the the longest running show on

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.510
the Discovery Channel was coming to an end
in 2016.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:44.429
For most of us, this was a complete surprise
given that the show was still as entertaining

00:00:44.429 --> 00:00:45.790
as ever.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:49.790
Since then, we’ve seen multiple spinoffs
emerge including MythBusters: The Search,

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:53.600
White Rabbit Project, Mythbusters Jr., and
Motor Mythbusters.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.559
While some of these were great in their own
right, it was of course never as good as the

00:00:57.559 --> 00:00:58.559
original.

00:00:58.559 --> 00:01:03.379
So, what happened to MythBusters and why was
the show cancelled?

00:01:03.379 --> 00:01:09.770
INTERNAL STRAINS:
While it may seem like MythBusters ended abruptly,

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:13.509
there was actually a slew of fundamental issues
that plagued the team for years.

00:01:13.509 --> 00:01:18.460
One of these issues was the chemistry between
the team members themselves, specifically

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:19.460
Adam and Jamie.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:25.229
Now, this might come as a surprise to many
of you, but Adam and Jamie aren’t actually

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:26.229
friends.

00:01:26.229 --> 00:01:28.740
And this isn’t speculation or a fan theory.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.729
Both of them have actually been extremely
transparent about how they don’t actually

00:01:32.729 --> 00:01:34.289
get along in real life.

00:01:34.289 --> 00:01:38.440
Adam said quote “We don't get along very
well together on a personal level.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.490
In 25 years we've known each other, we've
never had dinner alone together.”

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:48.090
Similarly, when asked if it would be an exaggeration
to say that Jamie didn’t really like Adam,

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.640
Jamie replied, “No.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:54.090
We certainly had respect for each other, but
we really weren’t friends.”

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:57.950
Considering this, it’s extremely impressive
that this duo was able to sustain such a productive

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.229
professional relationship for so long.

00:02:00.229 --> 00:02:04.119
But, if it was up to them, they wouldn’t
voluntarily work with each other.

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:08.660
In other words, the opportunity to work together
didn’t keep them on the show by any menas.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:13.020
They each had their own independent reasons
to do the show and when those reasons dissolved,

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.890
they didn’t hesitate to split ways.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:19.240
If you’re wondering about the relationship
betwen Tori, Kari, and Grant, these guys were

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:22.360
basically the exact opposite of Adam and Jamie.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:24.040
They got together extremely well.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.210
In fact, here’s what Grant had to say about
it.

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:30.000
“The three of us—you, Tory and I—we
are beyond friends.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.140
We are siblings.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:34.880
We shared a long, wild adventure, learning
from each other the whole way.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:39.190
Our cameraman nicknamed us Technical, Practical,
and Logical because we were so different,

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:41.510
but we could solve any problem together.”

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:46.390
Clearly, this trio liked working with each
other, but that wasn’t enough to deter them

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:48.290
from leaving the show when the time came.

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:52.540
You see, interest in Mythbusters was slowly
declining over the years.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:57.880
Now, I know it makes a lot of you guys upset
when I say things like this because yes, even

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.800
after the decline, Mythbusters was still super
popular.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.840
However, when you’re constantly trying to
produce bigger seasons with bigger myths and

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:09.400
bigger budgets, it’s not really sustainable
when viewership and ratings are declining.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.750
And according to data, the decline was pretty
clear.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.900
Take a look at Google Trends for example.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:19.820
The search data says that interest in Mythbusters
peaked between 2006 and 2008.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:25.590
There were two peaks in 2009 and 2011, but
for the most part, the underlying decline

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:26.590
continued.

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:30.640
And, by the time the show ended, it was only
pulling in 20-30% of interest that it was

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.690
pulling in during its peak.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:47.340
And if you don’t believe me, just listen
to Adam himself describe the issue.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:58.570
So, while Mythbusters was still quite popular
and adored by its super fans, the average

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.740
viewer was starting to tune out.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:04.710
And this makes sense given that the Mythbusters
had already tested most of the super popular

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:05.710
myths.

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:16.100
There’s only so many Jack and Rose scenes
and Walter White scenes that everyone knows.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:19.750
Sooner or later, you’re gonna have to tackle
less popular myths that aren’t as appealing

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:21.299
to the general audience.

00:04:21.299 --> 00:04:25.689
Eventually, this led to declining ratings
which started to take a toll on the show.

00:04:25.689 --> 00:04:31.590
THE COLLAPSE:
One of the first shortfalls that was extremely

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:35.650
evident to viewers was what happened to Tori,
Grant, and Kari.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:40.389
In 2014, it was announced that the B cast
would be eliminated and that the show would

00:04:40.389 --> 00:04:42.510
simply focus on Adam and Jamie.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:47.750
According to the producers, what Grant, Kari,
and Tory were asking for was unreasonable.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:52.520
We never really got a solid explanation as
to what exactly they asked for or why negotiations

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.090
didn’t end up fruitful.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:57.460
At first, there was some speculation that
this trio might’ve grown some resentment

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:59.590
for each other just like Adam and Jamie.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:04.599
But, they would soon turn around and star
in the White Rabbit Project together, so this

00:05:04.599 --> 00:05:06.340
likely wasn’t the case.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:10.970
The more likely scenario is that the trio
wanted to maintain their compensation or increase

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:11.970
it.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:15.569
And given that viewership was declining, this
simply wasn’t feasible.

00:05:15.569 --> 00:05:19.169
Something else to note is that it seems like
the trio also didn’t agree with the direction

00:05:19.169 --> 00:05:21.819
that the producers were taking Mythbusters.

00:05:21.819 --> 00:05:25.360
Instead of myths being at the center of each
episode, it felt like the producers wanted

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.729
more explosions and theatrics.

00:05:27.729 --> 00:05:31.780
They probably thought that this would help
retain viewers, but it kind of just caused

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:33.370
the show to lose its original appeal.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:38.650
Once Kari, Tori, and Grant were removed from
the show, ratings just declined even faster.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:42.120
While some viewers were indifferent to the
change, most viewers were upset that they

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:43.120
were cut from the show.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:47.210
They felt that the trio gave a healthy break
from the antics of Adam and Jamie.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:51.060
Also, Kari was the only woman on the show.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:55.659
And given that STEM fields are generally skewed
towards men, many young girls looked up to

00:05:55.659 --> 00:05:56.659
Kari.

00:05:56.659 --> 00:05:58.750
But, this ended with the elimination of the
B team.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:03.129
Moving onto the last two seasons of Mythbusters,
given that half the show was cut, the number

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:05.999
of myths tested per show was also cut in half.

00:06:05.999 --> 00:06:09.750
Each episode only covered 2 myths instead
of 3 or 4 like before.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:13.090
On the brightside, this allowed the producers
to spend more time showing the engineering

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:14.669
behind each project.

00:06:14.669 --> 00:06:18.509
Adam and Jamie also had more time to explain
the science behind each experiment.

00:06:18.509 --> 00:06:22.870
While these facets were welcomed by superfans,
to the average viewer, this likely just felt

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:25.279
slower paced and not as exciting.

00:06:25.279 --> 00:06:29.499
And soon enough, Adam and Jamie’s 5 year
contract was coming to an end as well meaning

00:06:29.499 --> 00:06:31.800
that that it was time to renegotiate terms.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:35.289
Adam was actually super transparent about
this stating that he simply wasn’t willing

00:06:35.289 --> 00:06:49.050
to the do show for less compensation.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:52.949
And given that Discovery wasn’t willing
to allocate a bigger budget, the only option

00:06:52.949 --> 00:06:54.469
was to shut it down.

00:06:54.469 --> 00:06:58.620
The silver lining is that Discovery let Jamie
and Adam end the show on their terms.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:02.919
They were allowed to call it a final season
and they were able to test some of the biggest

00:07:02.919 --> 00:07:03.919
myths yet.

00:07:03.919 --> 00:07:07.499
But, the best part of it all was that they
were able to invite Kari, Tori, and Grant

00:07:07.499 --> 00:07:09.229
to do a wrap up episode.

00:07:09.229 --> 00:07:12.879
This conclusion was extremely well received
by the fans given that it was the highest

00:07:12.879 --> 00:07:14.470
rated Mythbusters episode period.

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:19.400
So, while it was a shame that Mythbusters
came to an end earlier than people wanted,

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:23.650
it’s nice that the show atleast got the
ending that it deserved.

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:28.639
MYTHBUSTERS TODAY:
In terms of what the mythbusters are up to

00:07:28.639 --> 00:07:31.870
today, they’ve all gone down their own paths.

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:36.220
Starting with Adam, while he left mythbusters,
he never really left the show business.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:40.680
He went on to host two more shows called Mythbusters
Jr. and Savage Builds.

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.479
Given the name Mythbusters Jr., I don’t
think you’d be surprised to hear that it

00:07:44.479 --> 00:07:46.939
had a similar premise to the original show.

00:07:46.939 --> 00:07:50.400
Instead of having adults test these myths,
however, we had teenagers test these myths.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:54.979
And Adam was basically their mentor, leading
them through the design, assembly, and testing

00:07:54.979 --> 00:07:56.099
processes.

00:07:56.099 --> 00:08:00.879
As for Savage Builds, this show was focused
on a new inventions and restoration projects.

00:08:00.879 --> 00:08:04.539
Adam collaborated with industry experts and
friends to make things like the Iron Man suit

00:08:04.539 --> 00:08:05.839
and the Wheel of death.

00:08:05.839 --> 00:08:08.900
Savage Builds actually performed quite well
while Mythbusters Jr. performed alright.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:12.319
However, both of these shows were cancelled
after just 1 season.

00:08:12.319 --> 00:08:14.550
Adam wasn’t just involved in TV shows either.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:19.729
He also had a cameo in 2048: Nowhere to Run
and he published a book called Every Tool’s

00:08:19.729 --> 00:08:21.699
a Hammer: Life is what you make it.

00:08:21.699 --> 00:08:25.479
Likely, his most significant project over
past several years, however, is his YouTube

00:08:25.479 --> 00:08:26.599
channel.

00:08:26.599 --> 00:08:30.349
Adam became the face of the YouTube channel
“Tested” and they even renamed the channel

00:08:30.349 --> 00:08:32.039
to Adam Savage’s Tested.

00:08:32.039 --> 00:08:35.940
The channel has nearly 6 million subscribers
and they post a new video almost everyday

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.870
about science and building.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:42.010
Anyway, moving onto Jamie Hyneman, his life
after Mythbusters hasn’t been nearly as

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:43.010
eventful.

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:47.560
He has more or less left the show business
and has mainly focused on personal projects.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:51.030
For example, he built a tank that’s specifically
designed for firefighting.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:55.490
He also received an honorary doctorate in
technology from Lappeenranta University of

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:56.830
Technology in 2017.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.850
This was actually his third honorary doctorate.

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:03.130
He had previously received one from Villanova
University and the University of Twente.

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:08.960
More recently, he was appointed as a professor
at LUT University in November of 2021.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:12.500
This was a five year contract, so this is
probably where he’ll be spending the majority

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:14.220
of his time in the coming years.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:18.360
Moving onto Tory Belleci, he’s basically
just jumped from one show to another.

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:22.940
Shortly after Mythbusters ended, he started
hosting a show called Thrill Factor with Kari.

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:26.610
The show focuses on the science and engineering
behind roller coasters and amusement parks

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:29.860
and explains why certain attractions are so
thrilling.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:34.550
After Thrill Factor, Tory went onto host White
Rabbit Project with of course Kari and Grant.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:38.720
He took a few years off from the show business
after White Rabbit Project, but he eventually

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:40.900
returned in 2019 with The Great Escapists.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:45.370
Since then, he’s also appeared on The Explosion
Show and Jackass Forever.

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:48.070
So, things haven’t really changed all that
much for Tory.

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:51.260
The same thing can be said about Kari as well.

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:55.380
She of course also hosted Thrill Factor and
White Rabbit Project, but she’s done a few

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:56.910
things on her own as well.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:59.530
For example, she hosted Crash Test World.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:03.690
This show focuses on the tech capitals of
the world and how these various cities are

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:05.180
helping build our future.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:09.080
Aside from starring in these shows, Kari also
helped found an educational streaming service

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.080
called EXPLR Media.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:14.610
The streaming service is still super new,
so we’ll have to see how it plays out.

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:19.350
And finally, last by not definitely not least,
we have Grant.

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:23.230
After mythbusters and White Rabbit Project,
Grant went on to host the second season of

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:24.770
The Home of the Future.

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:29.310
As the name suggests, this show focuses on
futuristic homes filled with the newest tech.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:32.990
Grant also had a Cameo in the TV movie Sharknado
3.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:36.470
Grant hasn’t just been working on the front
end of moves and TV shows either.

00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:38.940
He has also spent a lot of time on the backend
as well.

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:44.870
For example, in 2017, he consulted with Disney
for six months to help them build better animatronics.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:50.270
While things were going pretty good for Grant,
he would unfortunately be hit with a intracranial

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:53.200
aneurysm in July of 2020 which took his life.

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:58.840
He was only 49 years old at the time which
leaves him with the most tragic ending.

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:03.950
THE MYTHBUSTERS EFFECT:
While its already been several years since

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:07.690
Mythbusters shut down, I’d be willing to
bet that the effect of Mythbusters will live

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:09.820
on for decades.

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:12.800
Mythbusters likely inspired millions of kids
and teenagers to persue careers in science

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:14.190
and engineering.

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:17.340
And who knows what these young minds will
come up with in the coming decades.

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:21.740
In terms of the show itself ending, it really
just came down to declining viewership and

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:22.740
a limited budget.

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:26.890
But, honestly, I don’t think it’s necessarily
a bad thing.

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:30.370
More times than not, we see shows go on far
way too long.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:34.720
Mythbusters was able to end off at a time
where viewers still wanted more which is why

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:39.810
all of us still remember it in such a positive
light even after all these years.

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:44.240
And I’m not sure if any other ending could’ve
have created such a lasting effect, but that’s

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:45.420
just what I think.

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:47.330
Did you watch Mythbusters growing up?

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:48.610
Comment that down below.

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:52.550
Also, drop a like if you’re glad Mythbusters
ended off strong.

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:56.170
And of course, consider joining our discord
community to suggest future video ideas and

00:11:56.170 --> 00:12:09.890
consider subscribing to see more questions
logically answered.

